        "virustotalUrl": "https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/1aefa1b42d8a480a4c66a8cf3bf49296d1cfd7d518df694b51096c19070c3909",
        "scanners": {
          "vt": {
            "status": "suspicious",
            "verdict": "suspicious",
            "normalizedStatus": "suspicious",
            "analysis": "Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: team-dispatch\nVersion: 1.0.7\n\nThe skill bundle implements a complex multi-agent orchestration system that performs high-risk system modifications, including the installation of background persistence via launchd, systemd, or cron (scripts/watch-install.sh) and the granting of broad agent execution permissions (allowAgents: ['*']) by modifying the global openclaw.json configuration (scripts/setup.sh). While these behaviors are aligned with the stated purpose of managing task timeouts and multi-agent dispatching, the automated setup of background services and the expansion of the agent's privilege boundary represent a significant increase in the host's attack surface.",
            "source": "palm",
            "checkedAt": 1773043621741
          },
          "skillspector": null,
          "llm": {
            "status": "suspicious",
            "verdict": "suspicious",
            "normalizedStatus": "suspicious",
            "confidence": "medium",
            "summary": "The skill's files and runtime instructions broadly match a multi‑agent orchestration purpose, but they ask the agent to perform system-level changes (create symlinks, write global configs, install a persistent watcher, restart the Gateway) while declaring no required binaries or credentials — that mismatch and the persistent background installation are disproportionate and worth manual review before installing.",
            "dimensions": [
              {
                "detail": "The name/description (multi‑agent orchestration, DAG dispatch, durable tracking) match the included assets: agent templates, project.json, watcher scripts, and many workspace files for subagents. Creating workspaces, copying templates, and wiring subagents into openclaw.json is coherent with the stated purpose.",
                "label": "Purpose & Capability",
                "name": "purpose_capability",
                "rating": "note"
              },
              {
                "detail": "SKILL.md explicitly requires the agent to run <SKILL_DIR>/scripts/setup.sh up front and to perform an environment detection phase. The instructions direct creating symlinks, writing ~/.openclaw/configs/team-dispatch.json and modifying openclaw.json (including setting main.subagents.allowAgents:[\"*\"]), creating agent directories, creating sessions/, rendering and installing a launchd plist / scheduled task, and restarting the Gateway. Those are broad, system‑level actions beyond mere orchestration logic and give the skill the ability to change agent permissions and install persistent services.",
                "label": "Instruction Scope",
                "name": "instruction_scope",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "There is no formal 'install' spec, but many local scripts and assets are packaged with the skill and the SKILL.md instructs running them (setup.sh, watch.sh, publish-clawhub.mjs). This is higher‑risk than an instruction‑only skill because code on disk will be executed locally. There are no downloads from odd external URLs in the provided files; the repo includes a local Node publisher and watcher scripts. Still, the package executes system commands (bash/node/python) but does not declare required binaries.",
                "label": "Install Mechanism",
                "name": "install_mechanism",
                "rating": "note"
              },
              {
